{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs","id":1394736,"title":"Ministry in the Camarilla, Banu Haqim in the Anarchs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-07T02:08:27-07:00","id":1394736,"title":"Ministry in the Camarilla, Banu Haqim in the Anarchs","content":"I\u2019ve Long since thought that there should be more Clans in the Camarilla. My one exception was always the Assamites, or the Banu Haqim as they are now called. Through out the ages they dedicated themselves to killing and diablerizing other vampires, even having to be hunted nearly to extinction by the Camarilla and cursed by the Tremere. If it Clan should be forever barred entry from the Camarilla, it should be them. In the books it\u2019s heavily suggested that they blew up the meeting with the Ministry and even aided in the attack on the Tremere Chantry, suggesting that the Camarilla leadership are complete imbeciles when it comes to their dealings with the Banu Haqim.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla and the Setites, now the Ministry, have never had any major struggles with each other, aside from the rivalries that all Clans have. They are sneaky and corrupt, which is what the Camarilla is really all about. The a ministry can use their position with the Camarilla to better control politics and corrupt the masses. Meanwhile, within the Anarchs the Banu Haqim can combat vampiric excesses as they often have and get a few more chances to kill at their discretion. <br /> <br /> Even from a Discipline perspective, things are more balanced with the Ministry in the Camarilla. Now the Anarchs have two Protean Clans and the Camarilla has two Blood Sorcery Clans.<br /> <br /> Changing how this turns out would take only a minor tweak to the canon events - the Camarilla discovers the Banu Haqim bombing plans (successful or not) and slap themselves in the face for ever considering associating with the Banu Haqim and welcome the Ministry in. I\u2019m not sure how important this reversal would be to the setting, it\u2019s only just happened, but I like it more than how the events played out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 06-07-2020, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T05:00:42-07:00","id":1394757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs#post1394736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve Long since thought that there should be more Clans in the Camarilla. My one exception was always the Assamites, or the Banu Haqim as they are now called. Through out the ages they dedicated themselves to killing and diablerizing other vampires, even having to be hunted nearly to extinction by the Camarilla and cursed by the Tremere. If it Clan should be forever barred entry from the Camarilla, it should be them. In the books it\u2019s heavily suggested that they blew up the meeting with the Ministry and even aided in the attack on the Tremere Chantry, suggesting that the Camarilla leadership are complete imbeciles when it comes to their dealings with the Banu Haqim.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla and the Setites, now the Ministry, have never had any major struggles with each other, aside from the rivalries that all Clans have. They are sneaky and corrupt, which is what the Camarilla is really all about. The a ministry can use their position with the Camarilla to better control politics and corrupt the masses. Meanwhile, within the Anarchs the Banu Haqim can combat vampiric excesses as they often have and get a few more chances to kill at their discretion.<br /> <br /> Even from a Discipline perspective, things are more balanced with the Ministry in the Camarilla. Now the Anarchs have two Protean Clans and the Camarilla has two Blood Sorcery Clans.<br /> <br /> Changing how this turns out would take only a minor tweak to the canon events - the Camarilla discovers the Banu Haqim bombing plans (successful or not) and slap themselves in the face for ever considering associating with the Banu Haqim and welcome the Ministry in. I\u2019m not sure how important this reversal would be to the setting, it\u2019s only just happened, but I like it more than how the events played out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Revised at least WW made a strong effort to present the Assamites as something different from the stereotype of blood crazed diablerists. In V5 ONE THIRD of the clan has joined the Camarilla, those who wish to keep their attachment to humanity (and the religious faiths they followed in life). These are NOT the blood crazed assassins you talk about (and btw, the Assamites were never &quot;hunted nearly to extinction&quot; by the Camarilla...) and the matter of them joining the Camarilla is well detailed both in BJD and in the V5 products. Given the story as presented it makes sense these schismatics were accepted into the Camarilla (some ofthe Tremere tried to stop that from happening because they felt threatened by other blood mages, but some others, like Meerlinda pushed to have them join, while the other clans understood the advantage of having a second clan capable of Blood Sorcery, diminishing the Tremere power, and then the Tremere splintering happened and they suddenly lacked the political clout to stop the &quot;Assamite merger&quot;). More importantly from the political point of view having the &quot;humanist&quot; Assamites join allowed the Camarilla to further their alliance with the Ashirra. The Assamites had always been the dominant clan in the Ashirra (folowed by the Lasombra... note how the Lasombra joined next?) and them joining meant a much easier deal for concluding a functioning alliance with the oldest functioning vampire sect of the world.<br /> <br /> The Setites had actually petitioned the Camarilla for joining but were rejected. Considering how they are the ideological foil of the Ventrue it makes sense, it makes even more sense if you consider how the Camarilla only wanted a new clan between them and the Assamites and choose the latter because of all the political benefits they brought to the sect (or to the majority of the Camarilla clans at least).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:21:17-07:00","id":1394803,"title":"","content":"The 2nd Edition Assamites have been retconned as a cult called the Web of Knives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T14:18:07-07:00","id":1394850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1394803#post1394803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 2nd Edition Assamites have been retconned as a cult called the Web of Knives.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Web of Knives existed long before V5, and the Assamites working for Alamut are not just Web of Knives assassins. Btw, IIRC Fatima was trained as a Web of Knives member.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T15:23:36-07:00","id":1394859,"title":"","content":"I think it's very simple,<br /> <br /> setites don't fit in any sect,<br /> in the camarilla, they're a threat to the masquerade and a constant source of trouble,<br /> in the sabbat, they're only a step above infernalists<br /> <br /> the reason they were included with the anarchs was probably to make them easier to include as player characters (time will tell if it works)<br /> <br /> <br /> assamites though, Revised made them a good fit for both sects,<br /> the reasons they didn't join the Camarilla were two:<br /> 1 - the Tremere<br /> 2 - assamites like diablerie, Camarilla don't<br /> 3 - nah, that's really it<br /> <br /> Revised made them into a sort of single-clan sect (intentionally or not),<br /> nice concept in theory, but not that great for gameplay<br /> <br /> v20 picked up the idea and tried to make it work by dividing the clan into 3 bloodlines (still didn't work)<br /> <br /> so v5 went 'fuck it' and had them join the Camarilla","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T16:34:53-07:00","id":1394871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1394850#post1394850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Web of Knives existed long before V5, and the Assamites working for Alamut are not just Web of Knives assassins. Btw, IIRC Fatima was trained as a Web of Knives member.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they were retconned as such by Assamites Revised.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1394859#post1394859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's very simple,<br /> <br /> setites don't fit in any sect,<br /> in the camarilla, they're a threat to the masquerade and a constant source of trouble,<br /> in the sabbat, they're only a step above infernalists</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't see why the Setites would not fit in fine with the Camarilla. They're an intelligent, influence-peddling group of erudite philosophers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T16:50:42-07:00","id":1394875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1394871#post1394871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't see why the Setites would not fit in fine with the Camarilla. They're an intelligent, influence-peddling group of erudite philosophers.</div> </div> </div> </div>they're a blood cult,<br /> blood cults are not officially recognized in the camarilla,<br /> <br /> which I assume is why they did the whole rebranding in V5<br /> or V5 changed the policies towards cults, don't remember which","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 06-07-2020, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T16:57:40-07:00","id":1394876,"title":"","content":"Blood cults may not be recognized by the Camarilla, but that is quite a bit different from being banned by the Camarilla. If the Ministry can play ball within the Camarilla system, then their superstitions or practices behind closed doors shouldn't overly concern the Camarilla leadership.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T16:59:30-07:00","id":1394878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1394875#post1394875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> they're a blood cult,<br /> blood cults are not officially recognized in the camarilla,<br /> <br /> which I assume is why they did the whole rebranding in V5<br /> or V5 changed the policies towards cults, don't remember which</div> </div> </div> </div>The Followers of Set actually had a standing invitation to join the Camarilla. Amusingly, the Followers of Set accepted it only to have their delegation assassinated. PROBABLY by the Assamites.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> BJD was setting up both the Followers of Set Civil War and also the Camarilla joining that ended up petering out. Interestingly, they almost were a V5 Camarilla clan but the Lasombra got picked by Paradox instead. They wanted to replace the two lost clans and the Banu Haqim got picked with the Lasombra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:00:58-07:00","id":1394880,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I agree with your analysis of the Banu Haqim and the Web of Knives. As for the Ministry, Setites basically worship their Antediluvian founder, and that\u2019s pretty much anathema (pun intended \ud83d\ude0a) to the Camarilla\u2019s official philosophy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:02:49-07:00","id":1394882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1394880#post1394880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I agree with your analysis of the Banu Haqim and the Web of Knives. As for the Ministry, Setites basically worship their Antediluvian founder, and that\u2019s pretty much anathema (pun intended \ud83d\ude0a) to the Camarilla\u2019s official philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, the Ventrue worshiped their Antediluvian. They just claimed he'd been killed.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla is enormously hypocritical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:05:32-07:00","id":1394883,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> also, the standing invitation you\u2019re talking about is because the Camarilla owed the Setites a life boon after the fall of Alamut, and it might have been seen by the Inner Circle as politically unwise to have the two clans side by side in the same sect (though you could make the same argument for the Banu Haqim and the Tremere...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:06:44-07:00","id":1394884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1394876#post1394876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood cults may not be recognized by the Camarilla, but that is quite a bit different from being banned by the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>they were definitely banned in the camarilla pre V5 (not sure about V5),<br /> blood cults were still active in the Cam,<br /> and setite cults were active in cam cities<br /> <br /> the difference was that the blood cult thing was tied with the setite's clan identity<br /> <br /> a Toreador blood cult would just be a fringe group that wasn't representative of the whole clan<br /> <br /> for the setites tho, the blood cults weren't a fringe group, it was pretty much the whole clan (same for the serpents of the light in the sabbat)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:08:47-07:00","id":1394885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1394884#post1394884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for the setites tho, the blood cults weren't a fringe group, it was pretty much the whole clan (same for the serpents of the light in the sabbat)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. They'd be, &quot;I don't see a blood cult here.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now the Camarilla has changed its perspective in V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:11:18-07:00","id":1394886,"title":"","content":"I have a <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/EpilepticTrees\" target=\"_blank\">weird thought</a>.<br /> <br /> Hardestadt was a... arguably, the... primary leader of the Camarilla, and a noted conservative who felt things in the sect were fine as they were. The Ashirra are to be ignored. The Anarchs are vile, but ultimately unimportant. The Camarilla rules over every vampire in the world, whether they know it or not. Antedeluvians are down the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memory_hole\" target=\"_blank\">memory hole</a>.<br /> <br /> There were other elders who disagreed with these positions. Most elders disagreed with Hardestadt on one or two points, a few with all of them.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hardestadt&quot; was actually Hardestadt the Younger who was impersonating Hardestadt the Elder.<br /> <br /> Sooner or later, someone somewhere was bound to figure out that Hardestadt the Younger seized control of the sect. Those in a position to discover this were also in a position to not want to embarrass the sect by revealing it. That said, something would have to be done. This could not stand.<br /> <br /> Hardestadt was assassinated by Theo Bell.<br /> <br /> The Brujah were promptly removed from the Camarilla, in a divorce of mutual loathing.<br /> <br /> Theo Bell is not put on the Red List.<br /> <br /> Theo Bell is said to be an emissary between the Camarilla and Anarchs, despite his manifest inappropriateness for the role.<br /> <br /> The Banu Haqim (assassins whose discipline spread includes Obfuscate abilities which allow them to hide their identity among witnesses) are accepted as a full clan within the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> If a group of elders wanted the False Hardestadt destroyed, what would they have had to pay the Banu Haqim to carry out the contract?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:12:14-07:00","id":1394887,"title":"","content":"Good point! Though the Ventrue are now run by the Directorate and are the chief proponents of the view that even if the Antes did once exist, they\u2019re now largely irrelevant to the nightly existence of the Camarilla in 2020 (the complete opposite of the Sabbat, who basically viewed them as ancient monsters to be hunted down for the glory of Caine).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:14:39-07:00","id":1394888,"title":"","content":"This isn't exactly a direct answer but just something that I do for my personal chronicles...<br /> <br /> The Settites have numerous factions and the Followers of Set likely represent a plurality of them through a vast number of different blood cults and heresies.<br /> <br /> The Ministry is a faction that has intentionally trimmed itself. First by removing the more blatant elements of Set worship and corruption and posing themselves as a mix of modern religious groups as well as philosophers aping religious symbolism akin to many Satanists, in order to join the Anarch Movement and gain acceptance while keeping the Inner Mysteries for those who can be gently brought through the putrification and purification of the process.<br /> <br /> Once a stable environment could be found for the spiritual-lite form of Settite philosophy, the inroads could be made into the Camarilla with the Ministry treating all references to Set as a historical metaphor instead of theological truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:15:55-07:00","id":1394889,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a> brilliant \ud83d\ude0a! I love your theory.<br /> <br /> Also, the Serpents of the Light are defo a blood cult. They just venerate Caine instead of Set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:15:56-07:00","id":1394890,"title":"","content":"The Camarilla banning belief in of service of Antediluvians was basically a retcon, Revised I believe, and I would have no problem re-retconning it. I mean, seriously, the Tremere directly served their 3rd generation founder. <br /> <br /> It's far more compatible with the Camarilla than a blood cult dedicated to Diablerie and essentially killing all other vampires, which really is contrary to a core principle of the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:16:18-07:00","id":1394891,"title":"","content":"The Assamites as all blood crazed assassins never made much sense when you consider that they are the majority clan in the middle east. Who are the Assamites working for in that region? Are they hiring each other to assassinate each other? And while they are the majority clan in that region, the other clans do survive and even hold court in cities with Assamite princes. Which wouldn't make any sense if all Assamites were rampant diablerists. Yes, they possess a craving for diablerie, but that craving is no more severe than the Brujah tendency to fly into a rage and rip you limb from limb.<br /> <br /> All vampires need to step lightly around each other. You aren't any less dead if you accidentally set off that Malk primogen's delusion that you are the hunter who killed his sire a thousand years ago than you are because an Assamite tasted your blood and lost it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:17:30-07:00","id":1394892,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11637_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11637\" data-vbnamecard=\"11637\">Gryffon15</a> I agree with your interpretation of the Ministry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:20:55-07:00","id":1394893,"title":"","content":"Thank ya, glad you like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:27:00-07:00","id":1394897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1394889#post1394889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, the Serpents of the Light are defo a blood cult. They just venerate Caine instead of Set.</div> </div> </div> </div>the cult worships some american serpent deity (quetzalcoatl I believe),<br /> but individuals may adhere to the noddist faith","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:27:03-07:00","id":1394898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1394891#post1394891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Assamites as all blood crazed assassins never made much sense when you consider that they are the majority clan in the middle east. Who are the Assamites working for in that region?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ashirra basically retconned the Assamites not to be the &quot;Middle East&quot; clan because that never made any sense whatsoever even with the addition of the Judges and Viziers. I never had a problem with them being a crazy blood cult because they didn't have to be a &quot;Big&quot; Clan.<br /> <br /> They were also not mercenaries prior to the Dark Ages, they only work for the Camarilla so the Camarilla won't come on down on them while they murder other vampires for their blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1394888#post1394888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't exactly a direct answer but just something that I do for my personal chronicles...<br /> <br /> The Settites have numerous factions and the Followers of Set likely represent a plurality of them through a vast number of different blood cults and heresies.<br /> <br /> The Ministry is a faction that has intentionally trimmed itself. First by removing the more blatant elements of Set worship and corruption and posing themselves as a mix of modern religious groups as well as philosophers aping religious symbolism akin to many Satanists, in order to join the Anarch Movement and gain acceptance while keeping the Inner Mysteries for those who can be gently brought through the putrification and purification of the process.<br /> <br /> Once a stable environment could be found for the spiritual-lite form of Settite philosophy, the inroads could be made into the Camarilla with the Ministry treating all references to Set as a historical metaphor instead of theological truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was how they were initially described but CULTS OF THE BLOOD CULTS indicates that they're harvesting the BECKETT'S JYHAD DIARY plot about the fundamentalists in the Followers of Set wanting to destroy all of the non-orthodox pagans in the cult like the Children of Dambala (Dambala isn't evil) and the Eris worshipers. Those groups got together and formed the Ministry.<br /> <br /> So there's now a much thicker divide in the Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-07-2020, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:32:12-07:00","id":1394900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1394878#post1394878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Followers of Set actually had a standing invitation to join the Camarilla. Amusingly, the Followers of Set accepted it only to have their delegation assassinated. PROBABLY by the Assamites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lies! Lies and slander I tell you! The Banu Haqim would never do politically-motivated assassinations!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:39:04-07:00","id":1394904,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think that the Assamites are dangerous assassins from the Middle Eastern perspective too. I see the Middle Eastern vampire world as not so different from the European one. You have the Ventrue being kingly, the Toreador being artsy, the Gangrel roaming around in the wilderness, etc. <br /> <br /> I don't like it being such an obvious open secret that the Banu Haqim assassinated the meeting with the Ministry too. It makes the Camarilla look like idiots for not even wondering if it was them and letting the plot succeed flawlessly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:39:18-07:00","id":1394905,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/cor