_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:42:42-07:00","id":1394909,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> exactly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:50:43-07:00","id":1394913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1394906#post1394906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> maybe the Camarilla didn\u2019t like owing a life boon to the Setites and was looking for a graceful way to deny them membership.<br /> <br /> This is fun \ud83d\ude0a.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they owe them a life boon?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1394907#post1394907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Camarilla probably had a majority doing the golf clap. They didn't really want the Ministry with them.<br /> <br /> They just didn't expect their loss to be the Anarch's gain..</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if any Clan wants any other Clan around. They are all treacherous and dislike each other. Creating and maintaining something like the Camarilla is an exercise and working with people who are out to get you and who you are out to get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T19:04:00-07:00","id":1394930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1394891#post1394891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Assamites as all blood crazed assassins never made much sense when you consider that they are the majority clan in the middle east. Who are the Assamites working for in that region? Are they hiring each other to assassinate each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>I missed this earlier, but I have to imagine that whole region of the world was filled with <a href=\"https://www.live5news.com/2019/10/30/man-hired-hitman-who-hired-hitman-who-hired-hitman-who-hired-hitman-who-hired-hitman-who-snitched/\" target=\"_blank\">news stories like this one</a>. (Headline: &quot;Man hired hitman, who hired hitman, who hired hitman, who hired hitman, who hired hitman, who snitched&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:14:35-07:00","id":1394957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1394909#post1394909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> exactly</div> </div> </div> </div>Btw, I love the quote in your signature. Is it from &quot;Outlander&quot;? If it isn't, it should have been used there...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:26:48-07:00","id":1394968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1394913#post1394913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would they owe them a life boon?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Setites were the one who revealed Alamut's location to the Camarilla. Which meant that they could hit the Assamites where it hurt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know if any Clan wants any other Clan around. They are all treacherous and dislike each other. Creating and maintaining something like the Camarilla is an exercise and working with people who are out to get you and who you are out to get. </div> </div> </div>True but the Camarilla has never ACTUALLY wanted everyone a part of it. See the way they handled the Giovanni.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:33:22-07:00","id":1394972,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3586_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3586\" data-vbnamecard=\"3586\">Alqamar Alaswad</a> it is!! Love that show \u2764\ufe0f.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:50:14-07:00","id":1394981,"title":"","content":"My comments, as always, are not on the V5 version of canon because I'm not following it. But like many things concerning V5, my house chronicle &quot;canon&quot; does intersect with it. So I'll still comment.<br /> <br /> I think that the old Independent Clans work best as major metaplot chronicle elements, not something available for every chronicle. Their membership is not &quot;open&quot; in the sense that there's a wide variety of playable character types in them. They have much more specific rules concerning the embrace (then again, I often think the same of Tremere), and their centralized leadership has a very specific goal in mind.<br /> <br /> I always viewed the Followers of Set having a much less openly hostile relationship to the Camarilla than the other Independent Clans. First, they were actually offered membership in the Inner Circle originally. Although the clan refused, I took it as meaning negotiations could be resumed later. Second, they have active enemies in the Sabbat, both as they are general enemies of the Antedeluvians (and this clan worships their antedeluvian) and as protecting the Serpents of Light who are active heretics. I also believed that as part of their facade as worshipers of the Wyrm, they had agents who were members of the Camarilla and Anarchs. And those agents were fairly loyal to their sects, except that their true loyalties were to their clan. In my own chronicles, I had an alternate name for the Clan (they were called the Rouquin which means red headed in French) and they were known to have lots of Camarilla &quot;members&quot;. Not fully trusted, but the Setites were playing a long game so their Camarilla members didn't stupidly betray everyone whenever they had a chance. And there were always rumors the clan was going to join the Inner Circle at some point. Of course, the Anarch &quot;members&quot; always disputed that, and the Independent &quot;members&quot; were ambiguous. They played this game for over five hundred years, and they could continue to play it much longer.<br /> <br /> The only interest I have in the Assamites is their role as an ersatz Assassins sect. There's a role for that in the game. It was obvious to me that they were NOT a generic clan of everything Middle Eastern. Even First Edition vampire made it clear the other clans were well represented in that region. It was simply bad writing that portrayed Assamites as pseudo-Muslims and thus everything Middle Eastern. When the game finally realized this and tried to retcon it, I think they made a mistake by creating all these sub-clans. It's fine for the Assamites to be limited in scope. You just needed to acknowledge all the other clans as being involved in the Middle East. In my head canon, the core concept of the Assamites is that they were possessors of an esoteric wisdom concerning the Caine figure, the Book of Nod, and every other lore associated with the origins of vampires. In their weird esoteric version of history and lore, they held certain heretical beliefs that caused all the other clans to hate them and view them as dangerous. So in reply, they began to kill other vampires - especially those they considered to be their enemies due to philosophical differences. (OK, another reason is that the whole Cain killing Abel thing, kind of implies it's OK to kill your fellow vampire brothers as well). That explains what they are, gives them some reason why they kill, and still provides some depth to them other than &quot;killers&quot;. It's limited in terms of playing one, but that's fine because they're a cult. They should be left as that. No reason for them to ever join another sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T00:34:25-07:00","id":1395028,"title":"","content":"The Camarilla claimed all kindred as it's members. It's just that some clans haven't organized a seat for themselves in the inner circle. <br /> Therefor<br /> I've always considered Followers of Set to be working with the Camarilla. Perhaps they have their own baronies, perhaps they have a presence in court, but they've never worked openly against the Cam, and they're good enough with prestation that their differences can be put aside. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla might've officially been against religion and the ideas of antediluvians (The acceptance of very low generations and clan founders is not the same thing as acceptance of a biblical &quot;antedeluvian&quot; child eating monster mythology) but the Settite doctrine was offering a completely different faith that doesn't really have that much relevance to others the same way Noddism does. <br /> <br /> The Assamites on the otherhand... I liked the schism as it was written in V20. I feel the Assamites would've mostly stayed in the nuCamarilla as they're very professionally minded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T00:57:12-07:00","id":1395032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395028#post1395028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla claimed all kindred as it's members. It's just that some clans haven't organized a seat for themselves in the inner circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>* And the Assamites were cursed by them<br /> * The Setites had an invitation but didn't accept it<br /> * The Giovanni were forbidden from being involved in all of Kindred politcs<br /> * And fuck the Ravnos.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla claimed all kindred but never believed or wanted it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Assamites on the otherhand... I liked the schism as it was written in V20. I feel the Assamites would've mostly stayed in the nuCamarilla as they're very professionally minded. </div> </div> </div>Technically, I think BJD retconned the Revised Schism and moved it down a decade. So they only joined the Camarilla in V5 not Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T03:10:21-07:00","id":1395047,"title":"","content":"Good thread!<br /> <br /> And to those who believe the Banu Haqim sabotaged the Ministry's attempt at joining the Camarilla? I can tell you that a lot of clans had something to gain by denying their admission. The Banu Haqim.. The Toreador.. The Ministry themselves....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T03:14:00-07:00","id":1395048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395032#post1395032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> * The Setites had an invitation but didn't accept it<br /> * The Giovanni were forbidden from being involved in all of Kindred politcs<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>When were these ideas introduced? <br /> (for the Setites, maybe that happened in times long gone, but I think you're refering to a modern invitation here, are you not?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T12:01:25-07:00","id":1395124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395048#post1395048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When were these ideas introduced?<br /> (for the Setites, maybe that happened in times long gone, but I think you're refering to a modern invitation here, are you not?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Revised Clanbooks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clanbook Setite Revised</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now you too know what could impel the Camarilla\u2019s founders to put aside their bigotries and offer the Followers of Set a place at the Camarilla\u2019s table. The Camarilla would have had an eighth clan, had the Hierophants accepted their offer. Bigotry and grievances, however, work both ways. Joining the Camarilla would mean renouncing Set\u2019s war against the clan founders who betrayed him, and that they could not do \u2014 at least, that\u2019s what the elders say.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clanbook Giovanni Revised</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather than see the other Kindred unite against them, the Giovanni agreed to remain forever outside of Kindred affairs. Known as the Promise of 1528, this agreement, I think, was an effort on the part of the Camarilla to shut down another Anarch Revolt before it could happen. By making the Giovanni essentially apolitical outsiders, they would isolate the Venetian family and its undead population from the other Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T13:38:16-07:00","id":1395138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395048#post1395048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When were these ideas introduced?<br /> (for the Setites, maybe that happened in times long gone, but I think you're refering to a modern invitation here, are you not?)</div> </div> </div> </div>V5, Anarch, page 182-183.<br /> Also, V5, Camarilla, page 160.<br /> <br /> Basically the Assamites schismatics and the Setites both contacted the Camarilla for admittance (at different times and for different reasons). The Camarilla held the decisive meetings to decide who would join and who wouldn't the same night in 2 different cities. The Setites met with the Camarilla envoys at an hotel in Paris that was hosting a NATO meeting. The Assamites meeting was in the kitchen of a non descript resturant in the small danish town of Odense. The Setite meeting blew up while the Assamite meeting went through.<br /> <br /> In Paris both the Setite representatives and the Camarilla representatives (a few Justicars including the Toreador one) were killed. The Setites in particular were said to have lost &quot;their most powerful members&quot;. Even after that event the Setites tried to contact the Camarilla to see if they could gain acceptance but were refused. Their only remaining option was to join the Anarchs so they did just that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 06-08-2020, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T14:50:11-07:00","id":1395155,"title":"","content":"So revised eh? <br /> A lot of people don't like that edition. I don't like this particular idea because, well, it's just really silly to promise to stay out of the politics of other kindred. That's like having a baby promise they won't grow up. . <br /> it doesn't really justify the Hecatta. (nor does toppling the Giovanni really justify the Hecatta) (Actually, nothing justifies the Hecatta as a clan. As a sect it's a bit on the fence) <br /> If the Hecatta have killed the Giovanni elders, and and no longer have some absurd plan with the shroud that they need to keep hidden, why not just join the main factions? <br /> <br /> As for the Settites<br /> they also had the option to stay independent... <br /> <br /> I get it, Settites are all &quot;fuck the demiurge let's tear this place down&quot; but, unless they can get all the anarchs in on that, it doesn't really work for them. A messier war with them remaining nuetral would be a better move than an easy war for the anarchs. Because once the anarchs win, without settite philosophy, they'll just make another camarilla. <br /> <br /> There's a lot of other really small things that I'm too tired to write about, but these are really strange moves. I've honestly never been that big on the necromancers; most of their shtick was that they kept out of the way, and I don't really understand how to use wraiths in vampire, not do the people who've been running my games. I ran a giovanni game once but that was by no means a traditional giovanni game (They wanted high humanity? Session 0 really should've been longer) otherwise I think I've seen more flesh eaters than clan johns. <br /> <br /> I just feel like they're trying too much to shake the setting. The Gio/Setites haven't gone the way they probably would have, and the assamite schism needs a rethink now that the cam has downsized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T15:17:11-07:00","id":1395160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395155#post1395155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So revised eh?<br /> A lot of people don't like that edition. I don't like this particular idea because, well, it's just really silly to promise to stay out of the politics of other kindred. That's like having a baby promise they won't grow up. .<br /> it doesn't really justify the Hecatta. (nor does toppling the Giovanni really justify the Hecatta) (Actually, nothing justifies the Hecatta as a clan. As a sect it's a bit on the fence)<br /> If the Hecatta have killed the Giovanni elders, and and no longer have some absurd plan with the shroud that they need to keep hidden, why not just join the main factions?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Hecata. And you keep ignoring facts and trivializing things in order to further your bias. The promise was about the Giovanni not joining a Sect and minding their own business. Not all the Giovanni elders were killed. Augustus' loyalists were, not the rest. People like Ambrogino Giovanni for example are still around. The Giovanni are still the most populous and prestigious bloodline inside the Hecata, but now they have to share. As for not having a crazy plan... the Endless Night actually had a decent chance of working (although the end result could have been very different from what Augustus expected) but in the end it failed. BUT... Given we know who the Capuchin is, who says they don't have another sinister plan up their sleeve? One they need the Hecata to accomplish?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the Settites<br /> they also had the option to stay independent...<br /> <br /> I get it, Settites are all &quot;fuck the demiurge let's tear this place down&quot; but, unless they can get all the anarchs in on that, it doesn't really work for them. A messier war with them remaining nuetral would be a better move than an easy war for the anarchs. Because once the anarchs win, without settite philosophy, they'll just make another camarilla. </div> </div> </div>The Setites are now called the Ministry because they preach their &quot;gospel&quot; to the Anarchs so yeah, they are spreading their religion to the Anarchs. And as I mentioned above the Setites TRIED to join the Camarilla before they joined the Anarchs. They were REJECTED. They also didn't want to stay independent anymore because they were being attacked in their ancestral domains by the Gehenna crusade and they were losing people because the vast majority of the Sabbat warbands were a very real threat for a single independent clan. So they petitioned the Camarilla for admittance... as I said it didn't go as they expected (or at least it didn't go as some of them expected...).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a lot of other really small things that I'm too tired to write about, but these are really strange moves. I've honestly never been that big on the necromancers; most of their shtick was that they kept out of the way, and I don't really understand how to use wraiths in vampire, not do the people who've been running my games. I ran a giovanni game once but that was by no means a traditional giovanni game (They wanted high humanity? Session 0 really should've been longer) otherwise I think I've seen more flesh eaters than clan johns.<br /> <br /> I just feel like they're trying too much to shake the setting. The Gio/Setites haven't gone the way they probably would have, and the assamite schism needs a rethink now that the cam has downsized. </div> </div> </div>Given the story as presented the way things went for both the Giovanni and Setites actually makes sense. One third of the Assamites joined the Camarilla, mainly for protection against Ur Shulgi and that makes a lot of sense too if you spend some time looking into it (or just read the pages for the V5 Camarilla book I pointed out in my previous post).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T16:14:45-07:00","id":1395168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395155#post1395155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So revised eh?<br /> A lot of people don't like that edition. I don't like this particular idea because, well, it's just really silly to promise to stay out of the politics of other kindred. That's like having a baby promise they won't grow up. .<br /> it doesn't really justify the Hecatta. (nor does toppling the Giovanni really justify the Hecatta) (Actually, nothing justifies the Hecatta as a clan. As a sect it's a bit on the fence)<br /> If the Hecatta have killed the Giovanni elders, and and no longer have some absurd plan with the shroud that they need to keep hidden, why not just join the main factions?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are, the Promise doesn't bind the Hecata, only the Giovanni.<br /> <br /> Mind you, why would the Cappadocians join a sect that left them to die? IN the Giovanni Chronicles, the Cappadocians attempted to join the Camarilla (and receive protection) only to be refused.<br /> <br /> Because the Camarilla has never cared about All Kindred. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Besides, it was like 10 years until the Promise was up anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get it, Settites are all &quot;fuck the demiurge let's tear this place down&quot; but, unless they can get all the anarchs in on that, it doesn't really work for them. A messier war with them remaining nuetral would be a better move than an easy war for the anarchs. Because once the anarchs win, without settite philosophy, they'll just make another camarilla. </div> </div> </div>Don't take this the wrong way but you create these elaborate conspiracy theories about the Tremere and Sabbat but when one's almost certainly canonical, you seem to miss it.<br /> <br /> The Setites joined the Anarchs to use the Brujah, Caitiff, and Gangrel as canon fodder against the Camarilla. Which they'll succeed at because the Setites are geniuses on a level with the Tremere. The Anarchs will start becoming more Sabbat like because what they've lacked is charismatic leaders, a consistent ideology, and genius thinkers.<br /> <br /> Which the Ministry has in spades.<br /> <br /> *Thulsa Doom cackles evilly*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-08-2020, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T16:42:06-07:00","id":1395173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395168#post1395168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't take this the wrong way but you create these elaborate conspiracy theories about the Tremere and Sabbat but when one's almost certainly canonical, you seem to miss it.<br /> <br /> The Setites joined the Anarchs to use the Brujah, Caitiff, and Gangrel as canon fodder against the Camarilla. Which they'll succeed at because the Setites are geniuses on a level with the Tremere. The Anarchs will start becoming more Sabbat like because what they've lacked is charismatic leaders, a consistent ideology, and genius thinkers.<br /> <br /> Which the Ministry has in spades.<br /> <br /> *Thulsa Doom cackles evilly*</div> </div> </div> </div>More like the Anarchs were the only option left for the Setites since the Gehenna crusade was decimating them and the Camarilla rejected their plea of admittance.<br /> <br /> As for the Setites being geniuses... some are, some are not, much like any other clan, Tremere included.<br /> <br /> And the Anarchs will stay as they are some might be converted by the Setites for sure but the vast majority is clever enough to know the serpents don't give out anything for free.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T16:44:52-07:00","id":1395175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395173#post1395173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More like the Anarchs were the only option left for the Setites since the Gehenna crusade was decimating them and the Camarilla rejected their plea of admittance.<br /> <br /> As for the Setites being geniuses... some are, some are not, much like any other clan, Tremere included.<br /> <br /> And the Anarchs will stay as they are some might be converted by the Setites for sure but the vast majority is clever enough to know the serpents don't give out anything for free.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always felt that was the opposite of how the Setites operated. They're effective because every Clan doesn't give away anything for free.<br /> <br /> The Setites do.<br /> <br /> The only thing they want is your soul and that's an easy price to pay.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T16:50:20-07:00","id":1395178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395175#post1395175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always felt that was the opposite of how the Setites operated. They're effective because every Clan doesn't give away anything for free.<br /> <br /> The Setites do.<br /> <br /> The only thing they want is your soul and that's an easy price to pay.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Their method is remarkably similar to the one employed by drug dealers all over the world (and I believe it's been referred as such in more than one book reguarding Setites): &quot;the first dose is always free&quot;, you'll pay with all you have got and then some once you are addicted though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T01:41:41-07:00","id":1395268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395160#post1395160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's Hecata. And you keep ignoring facts and trivializing things in order to further your bias. The promise was about the Giovanni not joining a Sect and minding their own business. Not all the Giovanni elders were killed. Augustus' loyalists were, not the rest. People like Ambrogino Giovanni for example are still around. The Giovanni are still the most populous and prestigious bloodline inside the Hecata, but now they have to share. As for not having a crazy plan... the Endless Night actually had a decent chance of working (although the end result could have been very different from what Augustus expected) but in the end it failed. BUT... Given we know who the Capuchin is, who says they don't have another sinister plan up their sleeve? One they need the Hecata to accomplish?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna be completely honest here: I don't see the relevance of this. A few Giovanni sticking around doesn't make a difference to the idea that &quot;The Giovanni&quot; got mostly killed off. I guess <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> hit a nail on the head with the idea that they're just rebranding to get around a treaty, but, although I'd see why the Giovanni would want it, I don't see why the camarilla would or why either side would respect it. <br /> <br /> My V5 &quot;conspiracy theories&quot; aren't really that elaborate. Quite plainly they're the path of least resistance. <br /> <br /> &quot;The ministrry&quot; is such a vague, Dystopian rebranding that it's not funny (well it is but it's not going to do great for recruitment). I honestly feel they'd have a better shot sticking with the followers of set. Other Vampires generally don't embrace the kind of people that fall prey to the kind of cults where everyone's wearing white.... <br /> <br /> ...and as I was writing I started thinking maybe you were completly right and, though most kindred won't become Followers, the Settites probably could take a third of the anarchs true believers in a decade and another third could become true believers in five. There's no anarch faction that's organized enough to really resist them. Set's teachings are so anarch it hurts. They probably could money-away the second inquisition problem for people that work with them, leaving to an even bigger majority as those outside are purged...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T01:57:01-07:00","id":1395269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395268#post1395268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna be completely honest here: I don't see the relevance of this. A few Giovanni sticking around doesn't make a difference to the idea that &quot;The Giovanni&quot; got mostly killed off. I guess</div> </div> </div> </div>You guess wrong because as stated above the Giovanni were NOT mostly killed off. They give the Hecata AT LEAST half its number and are explicitly stated to be the most popolous bloodline in the whole clan, besides being the one who holds all the money (including families like the Milliner cannibal bankers, of course) AND the most skilled at ghost summoning and control (other bloodlines specialize in other branches of necromancy).<br /> <br /> In the Hecata the Giovanni are still the number one clan, so your initial statement is simply wrong and I get the impression you actively search for justifications to hate on V5 going as far as to ignore and distort information given to answer your questions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T02:20:34-07:00","id":1395270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395268#post1395268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna be completely honest here: I don't see the relevance of this. A few Giovanni sticking around doesn't make a difference to the idea that &quot;The Giovanni&quot; got mostly killed off. I guess <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> hit a nail on the head with the idea that they're just rebranding to get around a treaty, but, although I'd see why the Giovanni would want it, I don't see why the camarilla would or why either side would respect it.</div> </div> </div> </div>CotBG basically said that the Harbingers of Skulls, rather than act like the True Brujah and blame the entirety of Troile's Bloodline/Augustus' Bloodline, took the imminently more sensible route of blaming those Giovanni involved in the Purge of the Cappadocians. This means probably the top 10% of the Giovanni. As the Harbingers of Skulls, they could never get the Giovanni leadership because they had too many resources and support. Then they realized the rest of the Giovanni hated their leadership because they were, well, a bunch of assholes like most Kindred except more so.<br /> <br /> So the Harbingers made an alliance with the other 90% and purged the top 10% before rebranding as the Hecata.<br /> <br /> As for re-branding, I'm not sure that really underscores it because the treaty was with Augustus Giovanni and his childer while this is the Cappadocians now in charge of the former childer of the Giovanni. The original Treaty of 1528 also was for 500 years.<br /> <br /> So, hilariously, it expires in 2028 anyway so does it matter?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Promise_of_1528\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Promise_of_1528</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T03:04:00-07:00","id":1395279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395270#post1395270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> CotBG basically said that the Harbingers of Skulls, rather than act like the True Brujah and blame the entirety of Troile's Bloodline/Augustus' Bloodline, took the imminently more sensible route of blaming those Giovanni involved in the Purge of the Cappadocians. This means probably the top 10% of the Giovanni. As the Harbingers of Skulls, they could never get the Giovanni leadership because they had too many resources and support. Then they realized the rest of the Giovanni hated their leadership because they were, well, a bunch of assholes like most Kindred except more so.<br /> <br /> So the Harbingers made an alliance with the other 90% and purged the top 10% before rebranding as the Hecata.<br /> <br /> As for re-branding, I'm not sure that really underscores it because the treaty was with Augustus Giovanni and his childer while this is the Cappadocians now in charge of the former childer of the Giovanni. The original Treaty of 1528 also was for 500 years.<br /> <br /> So, hilariously, it expires in 2028 anyway so does it matter?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Promise_of_1528\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Promise_of_1528</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Corrections:<br /> <br /> -No numbers were given, in the manuscript it's just stated that the Giovanni Elders that were killed were those most loyal to Augustus, which was probably a much smaller fraction than 10% of the whole clan.<br /> <br /> -In Cults of the Blood Gods, The HoS are said to have carried a grudge with the Giovanni NOT because they had persecuted their former clan but rather because the Giovanni killed Capadocius depriving them of the revenge they felt they deserved (in V5 the HoS have been retconned into a specific bloodline of assassins, spies and diplomats that was almost completely imprisoned into the underworld by Cappadocius during the Feast of Folly)<br /> <br /> -The HoS did not make a direct alliance with the Giovanni, the whole thing was orchestrated by the Capuchin. They are not HoS and aimed to reunite the varius bloodlines of the clan of death under one single clan, the Hecata.<br /> <br /> -The Capadocians are not in charge of the Hecata. I suggest you re read the part about the various organizations and power cabals that compose the leadership of the new clan. The Capuchin are the ones who made it all possible but they shy away from a direct form of leadership (doesn't mean thay don't know when and how to act though).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T03:09:54-07:00","id":1395281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395279#post1395279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Corrections:<br /> <br /> -No numbers were given, in the manuscript it's just stated that the Giovanni Elders that were killed were those most loyal to Augustus, which was probably a much smaller fraction than 10% of the whole clan.<br /> <br /> -In Cults of the Blood Gods, The HoS are said to have carried a grudge with the Giovanni NOT because they had persecuted their former clan but rather because the Giovanni killed Capadocius depriving them of the revenge they felt they deserved (in V5 the HoS have been retconned into a specific bloodline of assassins, spies and diplomats that was almost completely imprisoned into the underworld by Cappadocius during the Feast of Folly)<br /> <br /> -The HoS did not make a direct alliance with the Giovanni, the whole thing was orchestrated by the Capuchin. They are not HoS and aimed to reunite the varius bloodlines of the clan of death under one single clan, the Hecata.<br /> <br /> -The Capadocians are not in charge of the Hecata. I suggest you re read the part about the various organizations and power cabals that compose the leadership of the new clan. The Capuchin are the ones who made it all possible but they shy away from a direct form of leadership (doesn't mean thay don't know when and how to act though).</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I'm speculating. But most vampire clans are about 6000 numbers of people so 600 or so vampire deaths seems reasonable to me.<br /> <br /> 2. No, they said they were not hating the Giovanni because they killed Cappadocias but because they deprived them of their revenge. Persecuting the Cappadocians was the primary motivation in their revenge still.<br /> <br /> 3. We literally saw the meeting that began the alliance in Beckett's Jyhad Diary. The Capuchin was not there but it was the planned treason that Beckett witnessed but didn't understand.<br /> <br /> 4. You overstate the Capuchin's role in the clan's day to days.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T03:33:25-07:00","id":1395289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395269#post1395269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pedantry. How would any of this be me in &quot;<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">search for justifications to hate on V5&quot;. Do you think I'm that desperate for reasons not to like V5? It's not exactly slim pickings; I don't need to fabricate more things. Maybe you just need to step back a bit, take a deep breath, and start looking at things objectively. I was just convinced the setite-anarch alliance was a good idea; clearly I'm flexible. Your flexibility is the one in question</span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395270#post1395270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> CotBG basically said that the Harbingers of Skulls, rather than act like the True Brujah and blame the entirety of Troile's Bloodline/Augustus' Bloodline, took the imminently more sensible route of blaming those Giovanni involved in the Purge of the Cappadocians. This means probably the top 10% of the Giovanni. As the Harbingers of Skulls, they could never get the Giovanni leadership because they had too many resources and support. Then they realized the rest of the Giovanni hated their leadership because they were, well, a bunch of assholes like most Kindred except more so.<br /> <br /> So the Harbingers made an alliance with the other 90% and purged the top 10% before rebranding as the Hecata.<br /> <br /> As for re-branding, I'm not sure that really underscores it because the treaty was with Augustus Giovanni and his childer while this is the Cappadocians now in charge of the former childer of the Giovanni. The original Treaty of 1528 also was for 500 years.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Promise_of_1528\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Promise_of_1528</a></div> </div> </div> </div>1- Was the 500 year timelimit a rumour or an actual condition?<br /> <br /> 2: surely that's a lot more than the top 10%. I can't remember how long it actually took for them to eat the capadocians, but if they really stayed out of kindred politics, they would have much stronger ration of elders than that. What about the younger elders/Ancilae that would'be sided with the elders? Like, sure, they might've hated their bosses, but you would probably see the event as a 'The dirty Rosalini/ Milliners are after us Giovanni.&quot; Perhaps some of them had bosses they genuinely liked (it is a family organization after all) or the alternative is worse. Stability is generally prefered to risk and blowing up your own house with some outsiders is a lot of risk. I really can't imagine a 10% loss here. You'd lose about 40%.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T04:45:27-07:00","id":1395298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395289#post1395289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1- Was the 500 year timelimit a rumour or an actual condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a rumor in prior editions and a fact in V5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2: surely that's a lot more than the top 10%. I can't remember how long it actually took for them to eat the capadocians, but if they really stayed out of kindred politics, they would have much stronger ration of elders than that. What about the younger elders/Ancilae that would'be sided with the elders? Like, sure, they might've hated their bosses, but you would probably see the event as a 'The dirty Rosalini/ Milliners are after us Giovanni.&quot; Perhaps some of them had bosses they genuinely liked (it is a family organization after all) or the alternative is worse. Stability is generally prefered to risk and blowing up your own house with some outsiders is a lot of risk. I really can't imagine a 10% loss here. You'd lose about 40%. </div> </div> </div>I doubt more than 1/5th of the Giovanni Clan were actually Giovanni-Giovanni.<br /> <br /> If I were to think of any clan that would win the award of &quot;most pragmatic&quot; it would probably be the Giovanni. The simple fact is that they wouldn't have to LIKE the fact the Harbingers have exterminated their elders, they'd just have to not suicidally throw their lives away. In what is yet another, &quot;just like the Tremere moment&quot;, the majority of Giovanni Elders lost their lives in a single attack by the Second Inquisition on the Giovanni Mausoleum where Augustus Giovanni's torporous form disappeared [Loresheets state he was killed].<br /> <br /> The question is thus not, &quot;Would you fight for your still living relatives?&quot;<br /> <br /> The question is, &quot;Would you fight to avenge the dead ones?&quot;<br /> <br /> And even then, would you do it suicidally against a bunch of older than Christ ancients who are unaffected by the Beckoning.<br /> <br /> I imagine a lot of Giovanni are plotting revenge or their own takeovers but those will be over centuries as that's how Kindred roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-09-2020, 07:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T05:32:28-07:00","id":1395317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394736-ministry-in-the-camarilla-banu-haqim-in-the-anarchs?p=1395298#post1395298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a rumor in prior editions and a fact in V5.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I doubt more than 1/5th of the Giovanni Clan were actually Giovanni-Giovanni.<br /> <br /> If I were to think of any clan that would win the award of &quot;most pragmatic&quot; it would probably be the Giovanni. The simple fact is that they wouldn't have to LIKE the fact the Harbingers have exterminated their elders, they'd just have to not suicidally throw their lives away. In what is yet another, &quot;just like the Tremere moment&quot;, the majority of Giovanni Elders lost their lives in a single attack by the Second Inquisition on the Giovanni Mausoleum where Augustus Giovanni's torporous form disappeared [Loresheets state he was killed].<br /> <br /> The question is thus not, &quot;Would you fight for your still living relatives?&quot;<br /> <br /> The question is, &quot;Would you fight to avenge the dead ones?&quot;<br /> <br /> And even then, would you do it suicidally against a bunch of older than Christ ancients who are unaffected by the Beckoning.<br /> <br /> I imagine a lot of Giovanni are plotting revenge or their own takeovers but those will be over centuries as that's how Kindred roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again that's not exactly what's written in Cults. The funny thing is you correctly reported what's written in the book a few post above this. The Giovanni rebelled against Augustus' loyalists not all of the Giovanni Elders (example, Ambrogino Giovanni is still doing his thing and he's working with the Capuchin), the Harbingers did not have the power to overthrow the Giovanni. It was the Capuchin who brought the various bloodlines together and made the coup against Augustus possible. The Giovanni are still the dominant bloodline in the Hecata.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T19:58:41-07:00","id":1395512,"title":"","content":"One thing that's important to note is the Hecata is neither a Clan nor a Sect. It's a blood cult, which is a miniature sect based around a religious ideal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}